From 664546a42b1463b79de2635ba2e7fb6e7e22be95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:29:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 066/162] drm/panel: raydium-rm692h5: Add the 90, 120 and 144
 Hz modes

The downstream panel has four timings. They differ in the porches,
which only size the DSI link in command mode, and in a block of about
100 register writes (the downstream timing switch commands) that set
the panel's own refresh rate. The 60 Hz block was already part of the
init sequence.

List all four modes, with 60 Hz preferred, and send the block of the
mode being enabled. A rate change is a full modeset, so the panel is
re-initialised with the new block.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-raydium-rm692h5.c | 346 +++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 218 insertions(+), 128 deletions(-)

